<concept id="t00634">
	<title>Highway Driving Assist settings</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>highway driving assist (HDA)
					<indexterm>settings</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e03933">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03934">
								<image href="images/OCL4M055128N.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e03935">
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Driver Assistance</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Driving Convenience</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Highway Driving Assist</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>While the vehicle is <term translate="no">ON</term>, tap <menucascade><uicontrol>Setup</uicontrol><uicontrol>Vehicle</uicontrol><uicontrol>Driver Assistance</uicontrol><uicontrol>Driving Convenience</uicontrol></menucascade> on the infotainment system screen to set options for each function.</p>
		<p>If you select Highway Driving Assist, the function can help you maintain a safe following distance and the set speed as well as center the vehicle in your lane.</p>
	</conbody>
